      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Post Meeting Survey Questions FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are post meeting survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Post meeting survey questions are the short questions attendees answer right after a meeting ends, about whether it was worth their time and what should change. A typical set rates the meeting on a 1 to 5 scale and closes with one open question about the next meeting.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create post meeting survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Start with the decision the answers should feed, then write three or four questions around it. In Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>, you describe the meeting and who attends, and Emergent builds the survey and the database behind it. A follow-up prompt adds a question or changes when the survey goes out.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good post meeting survey questions for employees?\", \"a\": \"For an internal team meeting, ask about time and outcome before format. Was this meeting worth the hour? Did the meeting reach a decision on the main item? Did you get a chance to speak? What one change would improve the next one? Leave out questions about the room or the snacks unless they caused a real problem.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best time to send post meeting survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Send it within minutes of the meeting ending, while people still remember what happened. Post the link in the meeting chat before people leave, rather than emailing it the next morning. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/post-purchase'>post purchase survey</a> runs on a different clock: send it once the order has arrived, not at checkout.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can attendees answer post meeting survey questions anonymously?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Turn on anonymous answers when attendees report to the person running the meeting, as at an all-hands or a team meeting led by a manager. Leave names on for client calls and small working sessions, where you need to follow up with one person. Emergent puts no cap on responses, so an anonymous survey can go to the whole company.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many post meeting survey questions should I ask?\", \"a\": \"Three to five for a recurring meeting, and a single question when you survey the same meeting every week for a month. Save a longer survey for a one-off event such as a quarterly planning day, where 8 to 10 questions can cover each session in turn.\"}, {\"q\": \"What post meeting survey questions work for a virtual meeting?\", \"a\": \"Ask the usual questions about time and outcome, then add one about the call itself: did audio or screen sharing get in the way? Ask whether people had a chance to speak, since a few voices can fill a video call. For a one-to-many session with a presenter and an audience, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/post-webinar'>post webinar survey</a> fits better than a meeting survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"What post meeting survey questions should I ask a client?\", \"a\": \"Ask whether the meeting covered what the client came for and whether they know who owns each next step. Add a rating for the call and one open question about anything left unsaid. Keep it to four questions at most. In an app Emergent builds, each client's answers live in a database you own, ready to read before the next call.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I act on the answers to post meeting survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Read the open answers first, then find the rating that moved most since the last round. Pick a single change, make it before the next meeting, and tell attendees what it was. Before you cancel a recurring meeting, compare four weeks of ratings, because one bad week can be noise.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get more people to answer post meeting survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Send the link as the meeting ends and ask people to answer before they leave the call. Say who reads the answers, and send one reminder, not three. For a team social rather than a working meeting, a few <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/funny-questions'><a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/funny-questions'>funny survey questions</a></a> can open the survey on a lighter note.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
